# The Lonely Rover, solved by the rover: the windmill route in lonely-rover-opening, step by step, to watch and record.
# Run by HEROIC_INPUT_FILE (Main.Director.cs); recorded by tools/record-solve.sh. One step a line; '#' lines are comments.
# The clock: noon on sol 1 at 0 s; the relay passes at 03:00 each sol (55,484 s, then 144,259 s).
# Honest about the game today: building is free (parts appear from nothing: CONJURED), the generator and the bank are FOUND in the cargo,
# and the rover's own work is real: it cuts a road with its backhoe (every bucket dug and hauled by the arm, the drive by its wheels'
# real grip) down to the level rock shelf under the rubble (-44.98) and digs the bank free from its end (docs/plans/road-plan.md).
# Predicted from the headless runs of 2026-10-10: the road takes about 49 backhoe cycles and 23 hauls (4.5 m3), the bank is free after
# 3 buckets from the pad; the bank's cells pass 0 C in the evening of sol 1; the call goes out at the 03:00 pass on sol 2 or sol 3,
# whichever the bank is full for.
# Since Jolt runs at Mars's 3.71 m/s2, not Earth's 9.81 (owner, 2026-10-10), measured: the road 52 cycles, 23 hauls, 4.53 m3 (56, 24,
# 4.78 at 9.81: the lighter rover settles a little differently at each station), the bank free after 4 buckets (3), the drive up the
# slide 29.2 s + 11.2 s (28.1 + 10.5: its grip, mu g = 2.14 m/s2, is under the 2.5 m/s2 it is commanded to speed up at), cells past
# 0 C at 33,646 s, the call on sol 3. The rubble is unchanged (its slide always settled at the planet's g): the bank's cover 1.044 m
# at 280 s, the solar-panels crate's 2.148, boulder 4 still 1.78 m from that crate; the boulders, falling at 3.71 now, lie within
# 0.35 m of where they lay (boulder 10 moved most; boulder 5 is 7.70 m from the bank, was 7.74).
clock on
wait 60
caption Step 1/15: The crater rim came down on the cargo. The battery bank lies under {battery-bank:crate.cover:0.00} m of rubble at (254.5, 137.9). The rover is at (190, 140).
expect field battery-bank:crate.cover between 0.9 1.2
look 240 18 16 205 -60 140
wait 120

caption Step 2/15: Drive east up the slide toward the bank, between the hand-tools crate and the motors crate.
follow
drive-to 240 137.5 0.8
# no turn-to 270 here: it arrives heading about 263 (-97), and turning in place on this 26 deg rock slides it down
drive-to 249.8 137.9 0.4
look 200 22 9 252.5 -44 137.9

caption Step 3/15: The rubble round the bank lies at 25 to 30 degrees, as steep as the rover can grip. Under it, from x 251 to the crate, the rock is a level shelf. The rover cuts a road down to it: station {road:station}, {road:cycles} buckets, {road:dug:0.0} m3 dug, {road:hauled} loads carried back down to the shoulder.
follow
speed 4
build-road-to 254.5 137.9 20
speed 1
expect road done
expect rover wheels-clear
expect rover grade-along 249.8 137.9 below 27
look 200 22 9 254 -44 137.9

caption Step 4/15: From the end of its road the backhoe reaches the bank: it digs it free ({battery-bank:crate.cover:0.00} m of rubble left over it).
where battery-bank.crate
dig until battery-bank:crate.cover below 0.12 max 8 left
wait 90
expect field battery-bank:crate.buried below 0.5
where battery-bank.crate
caption Step 5/15: The bank stands free on the floor of its pit, dug out by the rover's own backhoe.
wait 120

# The vault round the freed crate. Freed, the crate is stood on the pit floor (MachineView.Burial): the where steps above printed its
# centre at (254.46, -43.532, 137.922) over ground at -43.872, and in another run (254.42, -43.600, 137.919) over -44.072 (the road's
# cut differs a little run to run): 0.34 to 0.47 above the ground. The enclosure's floor 0.09 above the build's origin, 0.5 m high,
# holds the crate's centre (the cells' point, WorldZones.Inside) anywhere from 0.09 to 0.59 above it, the crate's base at its floor. The rock and bin, the strip and the
# mirror keep their places relative to it as before (the rock 0.25 above the floor, the strip 0.46; the mirror at the same height
# in the world as before, -41.40: 2.47 above the new origin).
caption Step 6/15: CONJURED: a regolith vault round the freed bank on the pit floor (building is free in the game today).
build new 254.5 137.9
look 200 25 8 254.5 -43 137.9
build (enclosure vault #:at (0 0.09 0) #:size-x 0.5 #:size-y 0.5 #:size-z 0.5 #:pressure 610 #:temperature -55 #:ground -55)
wait 60
caption Step 7/15: CONJURED: 40 kg of basalt in a lidded bin on the vault floor, and a brass-steel strip that opens the lid while the vault is cold.
build (heat-store rock #:at (0.12 0.34 0) #:mass 40 #:contents basalt #:temperature -55)
wait 30
build (heat-bin bin #:at (0.12 0.34 0) #:holds rock #:leak 0.1)
wait 30
build (bimetal strip #:at (-0.19 0.55 0) #:senses vault #:drives bin #:layers (brass steel))
wait 45
caption Step 8/15: CONJURED: a 4 m² mirror aimed at the rock. The afternoon sun heats the rock; the rock keeps the bank warm through the night.
build (mirror heliostat #:at (0 2.47 -3) #:area 4 #:onto rock)
look 200 20 10 254.5 -42 136
wait 75
build done
wait 30
expect built built-1 5
expect zone battery-bank.cells built-1.vault

caption Step 9/15: The vault holds the found bank's cells ({battery-bank:cells.temperature:0.0} °C). Now to the wind corridor at (180, 105), 80 m west and north: back down the road first (it cannot turn in its cut).
follow
back-to 246 137.8
# up the shoulder side of the way it came: the heaps it hauled lie along the downhill side (z 136 to 137.5, x 229 to 241)
drive-to 244 138.6 0.8
drive-to 226 138.6 0.8
drive-to 195 136 0.8
drive-to 180 113 0.5
expect rover near 180 113 0.8
turn-to 0

caption Step 10/15: CONJURED: a 10.6 m post and 10 m sails in the corridor's wind.
build new 180 105
look 0 15 24 180.4 -57.5 104.5
build (post tower #:at (0.45 0 -1.45) #:size-y 10.6 #:size-x 0.6 #:size-z 0.6)
wait 45
build (windmill sails #:at (0 11 0))
wait 75
caption Step 11/15: CONJURED: four 72:18 gear stages, 4:1 each, 256:1 in all, so the slow sails turn the salvaged motor past its 1,500 rpm cut-in.
look 180 12 3 180.45 -52.45 103.6
build (wheel wheel-a #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-72 #:at (0 11 -1.3))
build (arbor sails wheel-a)
wait 20
build (wheel pinion-b #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-18 #:at (0.225 11 -1.3))
build (mesh wheel-a pinion-b)
wait 30
build (wheel wheel-b #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-72 #:at (0.225 11 -1.4))
build (arbor pinion-b wheel-b)
wait 20
build (wheel pinion-c #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-18 #:at (0.45 11 -1.4))
build (mesh wheel-b pinion-c)
wait 30
build (wheel wheel-c #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-72 #:at (0.45 11 -1.5))
build (arbor pinion-c wheel-c)
wait 20
build (wheel pinion-d #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-18 #:at (0.675 11 -1.5))
build (mesh wheel-c pinion-d)
wait 30
build (wheel wheel-d #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-72 #:at (0.675 11 -1.6))
build (arbor pinion-d wheel-d)
wait 20
build (wheel pinion-e #:catalogue involute-gear-m5-18 #:at (0.9 11 -1.6))
build (mesh wheel-d pinion-e)
wait 60
build done
wait 30
expect built built-2 10
look 20 12 26 180.4 -57.5 104.5
wait 120

caption Step 12/15: FOUND: the motors crate holds a salvaged generator. A shaft from the last pinion to its rotor, then a wire from the generator to the bank.
join-gesture built-2.pinion-e motors.rotor
expect link shaft built-2.pinion-e motors.rotor
join-gesture motors.motor battery-bank.bank
expect link wire motors.motor battery-bank.bank
follow
wait 60

caption Step 13/15: Sleep until the bank is above 0 °C (it charges only between 0 and 45 °C). Predicted about 21:30 on sol 1 (the freed crate went into its vault at -63 °C).
look 200 22 9 254.5 -41.9 137.9
sleep-budget 60
sleep until cells.temperature above 0 limit 40000 paused
expect field battery-bank:cells.temperature above 0
expect field battery-bank:scene.elapsed between 25000 40000
caption Step 14/15: Sleep until the bank is full ({battery-bank:bank.charge:0} Wh now). While the machines are paused the generator charges at its last steady rate or, with none yet, an estimate from the wind and the gears: an approximation the sleep panel names.
wait 60
sleep until bank.full above 0.5 limit 150000 paused
expect field battery-bank:bank.charge above 499.9
caption Step 15/15: Full ({battery-bank:bank.charge:0} Wh) and warm ({battery-bank:cells.temperature:0.0} °C). Sleep until the call goes out: the relay passes for ten minutes from 03:00 each sol.
look 20 12 26 180.4 -57.5 104.5
wait 60
sleep until bank.won above 0.5 limit 150000 paused
expect field battery-bank:bank.won above 0.5
caption THE CALL WENT OUT on sol {battery-bank:scene.sol:0}, in the 03:00 relay pass. The rover cut its road and dug the bank free with its own backhoe; the vault, mill, gears and mirror were conjured; the generator and the bank were found.
wait 240
quit
